  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 228 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nOverall hot and mostly dry conditions are expected for our area next \nweek. The upper high will be centered over Oklahoma on Monday before \nexpanding northeast across the mid-South Tuesday. On Wednesday the \nhigh is forecast to become elongated from the Carolinas across the \nsouthern Plains and into the Southwest. Beyond midweek the medium \nrange models have some differences on the strength of the high and \nwhere it will be centered relative to our area. In addition to how \nit could influence temperatures (how hot), this will have \nimplications on whether a weakness or possible disturbances aloft \ncan bring any chances of showers and thunderstorms to our area. \nBlend of models at this time has daily highs generally ranging from \nthe mid 90s in our southern counties, to the upper 90s to 101 across \nthe Big Country and portions of the Concho Valley. PoPs are rather \nlimited and confined to portions of our southern counties.",
